{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a466c16eabfd85eaa3c5c5e1ed6cab3a27d200c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}=\\overline{BC}$\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95eaca439ccbf2863a43b05f4de566ccdabdc392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is 11 units long. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is congruent to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3d74045abcfa098fd661ad0693fc7461570ad63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ECD$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />. What is the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b49c3097ed0eacc7cdb3ab3850b7fdf1f67d407.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); draw((0,0)--(2,4)--(4,0)--(6,4)--cycle--(4,0),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (2,4), N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (4,0), SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, shift(0.2,0.1)*intersectionpoint((0,0)--(6,4),(2,4)--(4,0)), N); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, (6,4), NE);[/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3faeebd827a737fe303cfd780655ba68f0a1927e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4.5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5.5\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is congruent to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3d74045abcfa098fd661ad0693fc7461570ad63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ECD$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d5f6b57cdeb9817d21ce9a78245eb685d27edc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CE} =11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a8200762391e372bf0111baf76618d6bba846b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a466c16eabfd85eaa3c5c5e1ed6cab3a27d200c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}=\\overline{BC}$\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be36f1db2ebc5a5bff7dfa0b15c78291e6aaf7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />. Because point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd00009e9ce6ebf648dac581ab8ba030bad99e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}=\\frac{\\overline{BC}}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5.5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"230\" height=\"43\" />. We can say this because of CPCTC; corresponding parts of congruent triangles are congruent.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HzzzRJEppRA\">https://youtu.be/HzzzRJEppRA</a> Soo, DRMS, NM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=2124\">https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=2124</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bRJ_ghuH5qs\">https://youtu.be/bRJ_ghuH5qs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 8\">2006 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit